<task id="015" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-06a upload fidelity branch (original-if-unedited)</title>
    <phase>1 Entry</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>12</estimated-hours>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <dependencies>013</dependencies>
    <blocks>017</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api,frontend,spe</tags>
    <rigor-hint reason="Modifies save byte-persistence path (.cs + .ts); fidelity-sensitive; FULL per TASK-INDEX">FULL</rigor-hint>
    <model-tier reason="Bounded branch on an existing save path (persist original vs regenerate); no architectural blast radius">sonnet</model-tier>
    <parallel-group>W2b</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe reason="Save byte-selection logic is separate from the 010/011/012 mount edits and from 013's creation backbone; edits a distinct branch of the save path">true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    On first Save of an uploaded-then-mounted file, WHICH bytes persist to SPE depends on whether the user
    edited: if the upload is saved UNEDITED, persist the pristine ORIGINAL upload bytes (byte-identical);
    once EDITED, persist the regenerated `.docx` from editor state via `tipTapToDocxBytes(editor)` (the
    as-built save path). This is FR-06a. The regeneration path already exists (docxBridge +
    `PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` save); this task adds the unedited-original branch: track dirty state and,
    when clean, upload the retained original bytes instead of regenerating (avoiding the lossy mammoth
    round-trip for untouched files).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Full-stack developer fluent in the Compose save path (client dirty-tracking + `tipTapToDocxBytes`) and
    the BFF SPE persistence (SpeFileStore facade). You add a bounded conditional branch to an existing
    save path.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Upload -&gt; Save WITHOUT editing persists the pristine original upload bytes to SPE (byte-identical);
    upload -&gt; edit -&gt; Save persists the regenerated `.docx` reflecting edits. The branch keys off the
    editor's dirty state; the regeneration path is unchanged.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      As-built (design.md §2.7d): the save path already regenerates `.docx` from editor via
      `tipTapToDocxBytes` (option (b)) and load converts via mammoth `docxToTipTapHtml` (inherently lossy).
      FR-06a preserves fidelity for the common "uploaded, reviewed, saved unchanged" case by persisting the
      retained original bytes when the editor is clean. Depends on 013 (the create-on-save persistence path
      the branch feeds).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="save-persist" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file purpose="regenerate" edit="false">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/utils/docxBridge.ts</file>
      <file purpose="dirty-tracking" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</file>
      <file purpose="editor-dirty" edit="false">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <notes>
      `tipTapToDocxBytes` is at docxBridge.ts ~line 145. ComposeEditor exposes an `onDirtyChange` channel;
      ComposeWorkspace already tracks dirty state. The retained original upload bytes come from the 012
      upload-mount path (or 010 Browse bytes) — persist those when clean.
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SPE writes go through the SpeFileStore/Infrastructure facade; no `Microsoft.Graph` types leak up.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-005">Persist to the SPE container resolved in create-on-save (013).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Client save fetch uses `@spaarke/auth`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Unedited upload -&gt; persist ORIGINAL bytes byte-identical; edited -&gt; persist regenerated `.docx`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT alter the existing regeneration path for the edited case (matches §1.6 fidelity boundary).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">BFF-touching — measure publish-size delta vs 49.63 MB baseline; run CVE scan; add/update tests per §10.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose/save-fidelity, spe-persistence, tiptap-docx</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-005-flat-storage.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <justification component="Unedited-original save branch (extends existing save path)">
    <existing>The save path already regenerates via `tipTapToDocxBytes`; the editor already reports dirty; original upload bytes are retained by the 012/010 mount.</existing>
    <extension>Add a dirty-state conditional that persists retained original bytes when clean; no new service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, saving an untouched upload runs it through the lossy mammoth round-trip and mangles formatting the user never edited — a concrete fidelity regression FR-06a exists to prevent.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load spec.md FR-06a. Read the save path (`PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` + client save), `tipTapToDocxBytes`, and the dirty-tracking channel.</step>
    <step order="1">Ensure the retained original upload bytes are available at Save time (from the 010/012 mount).</step>
    <step order="2">Branch on editor dirty state: clean -&gt; persist retained original bytes byte-identical; dirty -&gt; persist regenerated `.docx` via the existing path.</step>
    <step order="3">Persist to the container resolved by create-on-save (013) through the SpeFileStore facade.</step>
    <step order="4">Add tests: unedited save byte-identical to upload; edited save reflects edits. Build BFF + package; measure publish-size; CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="5">Run code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ComposeServiceUploadFidelityTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Upload -&gt; Save without editing persists SPE bytes byte-identical to the uploaded file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Upload -&gt; edit -&gt; Save persists a regenerated `.docx` reflecting the edits (existing path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The branch keys off the editor's dirty state; a clean editor never triggers regeneration.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Persistence targets the container resolved by create-on-save (013) via the SpeFileStore facade; no `Microsoft.Graph` leak (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(negative) A whitespace-only / no-op edit that does not set dirty still persists the original (no spurious regeneration).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish-size delta reported vs 49.63 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE; unit tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
